# Copy to .env.dashboard and fill in. Gitignored — never commit it.
#
# This file is loaded with docker compose `env_file`, which does NOT do variable
# interpolation. That is why it exists: it keeps ETORO_USER_KEY (in .env) out of the
# internet-facing container, and it is immune to compose eating `$` in a value. Do not
# move these into .env.
#
# Do not quote the values here — env_file treats quotes as part of the value.

# scrypt hash of your dashboard password, in the form saltHex:hashHex (no `$`, so
# nothing in the env plumbing can mangle it). Password must be 12+ characters.
# Generated for you by bin/dashboard-secrets.sh — you should not need to write this by hand.
#   bin/dashboard-secrets.sh
# Paste the printed hash. Never store the password itself.
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD_HASH=

# Signs the session cookie. At least 32 characters:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Changing this invalidates every existing session — that is how you force a re-login
# if you ever think the cookie leaked.
JWT_SECRET=
